/*
    `\` is such-that. It is left-declarative: it introduces a local scope, the LEFT
    operand declares into it, and the right operand is a proposition over those names.
    The value is the value of the left operand for those values satisfying the right.
    This one construct is simultaneously a set, a partial description and a search,
    which is why refinement needs no separate language feature.
*/

{ int x \ x != 0 }
